# What each of the twelve territories has, per resource.
#
# **Generated from `releases/first-release.md` -> *Biomes*, and not edited.** `spec/planet.md`:
# *a territory's biome gives it its total capacity and density for each resource. Two
# territories with the same biome have the same numbers.* So this file states no number of
# its own - every line is its territory's biome, looked up.
#
# It went out of step twice before that rule existed, because the link was a table heading
# and a heading is not where a rule lives - `S-45`. `the_scenario_gives_each_territory_what
# _its_biome_gives_it` reads the release and holds all twelve, so the next divergence fails
# rather than being read wrongly by a person deriving the dump by hand.
#
# `5 x 6` is total capacity for five extractors, each yielding six.


# territory 1: grassland
set resource 1 food 5 6
set resource 1 metal 2 3
set resource 1 energy 1 3

# territory 2: grassland
set resource 2 food 5 6
set resource 2 metal 2 3
set resource 2 energy 1 3

# territory 3: grassland
set resource 3 food 5 6
set resource 3 metal 2 3
set resource 3 energy 1 3

# territory 4: mountain
set resource 4 food 1 3
set resource 4 metal 5 7
set resource 4 energy 2 3

# territory 5: mountain
set resource 5 food 1 3
set resource 5 metal 5 7
set resource 5 energy 2 3

# territory 6: jungle
set resource 6 food 6 6
set resource 6 metal 1 2
set resource 6 energy 1 2

# territory 7: jungle
set resource 7 food 6 6
set resource 7 metal 1 2
set resource 7 energy 1 2

# territory 8: grassland
set resource 8 food 5 6
set resource 8 metal 2 3
set resource 8 energy 1 3

# territory 9: mountain
set resource 9 food 1 3
set resource 9 metal 5 7
set resource 9 energy 2 3

# territory 10: desert
set resource 10 food 2 4
set resource 10 metal 3 4
set resource 10 energy 5 6

# territory 11: grassland
set resource 11 food 5 6
set resource 11 metal 2 3
set resource 11 energy 1 3

# territory 12: ice
set resource 12 food 1 2
set resource 12 metal 3 5
set resource 12 energy 1 2
